"""Hacker Protocol for 355PM.

Fires DEBIT-SPREAD hackers at half the parent's filled size to partially unwind
350PM positions when the 3:55 SPX imbalance is adversarial to that fill. Targets
(TARGET_NAMES): every 350PM SPX credit-spread-sale strategy WIDER than $10 -- the
10 parents (all prod SPREAD_SALES_SPX configs except the $10-wide BASE and LOW_VIX),
the 2 CLOSER variants ($5-wide, kept deliberately), and the 3 BUMPED strategies.
NDX strategies are EXPLICITLY excluded (different underlying; the adversarial gate
is the SPX 355 imbal). Parents added 2026-08-31; bumped added 2026-08-20.

Three entry points, imported by 355pm_script.py:

  query_closer_fills(today, is_test, test_hack_rows, log_fn)
      Called at 3:54:50. Queries optionsResearch.algo_trade_log for today's
      TARGET_NAMES fills and returns a list of raw fill dicts. In test mode with
      TEST_HACK non-empty, bypasses the DB and uses the caller's rows.

  fire_hackers(trade_dict, hacker_fills, factor_..., factor_..., puts, calls,
               today, is_test, log_fn, delay_start_seconds=0.10)
      Called concurrently with orchestrate_batched_send via asyncio.gather. Sleeps
      delay_start_seconds so orchestrator's wave-1 hits SR first, then filters
      adversarial fills and fires all surviving hackers concurrently via
      send_complex_two_waves (then wave-3 rest, see below). Appends fired hacker
      trades (with grouping_codes) to trade_dict so the main-script log_trades
      call picks them up naturally.

  refresh_hacker_fills(trade_dict, factors, script_name)
      Called after the main log_trades pass. If any hacker carries a wave-3
      resting order (which can fill any time up to 16:00, after the main 60s fill
      snapshot), sleeps until ~16:00:30 ET and re-UPSERTs just the hacker rows in
      algo_trade_log so their fills are final. No-op on non-hack days.

Adversarial gate:
  Put  fill -> requires factor_355_imbal_less_than_neg_950m == 1
  Call fill -> requires factor_355_imbal_greater_than_950m  == 1
  (950M gate since 8/21/26: 1B research threshold minus a live-vs-T+1 jitter buffer;
  the hacking backtest stays at 1B.)

Debit-spread leg mapping (buy back the parent's short leg, sell back the long):
  hacker.long_legs  = leg at parent's short_strike  (BUY)
  hacker.short_legs = leg at parent's long_strike   (SELL)

Price cap + wave-3 rest: min_price = -HACK_MAX_PRICE clamps every wave's limit, so we
pay at most HACK_MAX_PRICE per spread (natural cheaper -> we pay the cheaper price).
After the standard two waves (~6s), any unfilled remainder is re-sent as a WAVE-3
resting order at exactly -HACK_MAX_PRICE with orderDuration = seconds to 16:00:00,
so the bid stays working server-side at SR until the close (backtest 8/31/26: most
of the hack edge above the cap comes back to us later in the 15:55-16:00 window).
"""

